# `npm install` and `npm ci` both fail on a clean checkout without this.
#
# openapi-typescript (7.13.0, its latest) still declares `typescript: ^5.x`
# as a peer, and this project builds on typescript ~6.0.2 -- npm's default
# strict peer resolution calls that a conflict and refuses to install
# anything at all. The tool works fine under 6: `npm run api:generate`
# regenerates src/api/schema.d.ts byte-for-byte identically, so the peer
# range is stale, not a real incompatibility.
#
# npm's own `overrides` would be the narrower fix, but every form of it
# (nested, top-level, `$typescript`) crashes arborist on npm 10.x with
# "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'edgesOut')". This setting is
# the one remedy that works on every npm version, and committing it means
# no contributor has to discover the flag for themselves.
#
# Revisit when openapi-typescript widens its peer range to include 6.x.
legacy-peer-deps=true
